              "explanation": "MSFT 68.8%, KO 61.0%, COST 12.8%.",
              "source": {
                "ticker": "MSFT",
                "fy": 2025,
                "metrics": [
                  "gross_margin"
                ],
                "formula": "gross_profit / revenue"
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "u1-l2",
          "title": "Operating & net margin",
          "xp": 10,
          "intro": "# Below the gross line\n\nAfter the cost of goods come salaries, rent, R&D and marketing. What remains is **operating income**. Then interest and taxes leave **net income**.\n\n- Operating margin = operating income / revenue\n- Net margin = net income / revenue\n\nMargins can be negative when a company loses money.",
          "questions": [
            {
              "id": "q-u1l2-1",
              "type": "numeric",
              "prompt": "Apple earned $133.1B of operating income on $416.2B of revenue. Operating margin in %?",
              "answer": 0.319798,
              "tolerance": 0.005,
              "unit": "percent",
              "explanation": "$133.1B / $416.2B = 32.0%.",
              "source": {
                "ticker": "AAPL",
                "fy": 2025,
                "metrics": [
                  "operating_margin"
                ],
                "formula": "operating_income / revenue"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "q-u1l2-2",
              "type": "multiple_choice",
              "prompt": "Ford had $-2.0B net income on $187.0B revenue. What's its net margin?",
              "choices": [
                "1.1%",
                "2.7%",
                "-1.1%",
                "10.2%"
              ],
              "answer": 2,
              "unit": "percent",
              "explanation": "Net margin = $-2.0B / $187.0B = -1.1%. A loss makes the margin negative.",
              "source": {
                "ticker": "F",
                "fy": 2025,
                "metrics": [
                  "net_margin"
                ],
                "formula": "net_income / revenue"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "q-u1l2-3",
              "type": "true_false",
              "prompt": "True or false: a company's operating margin is always lower than its gross margin.",
              "answer": true,
              "unit": "none",
              "explanation": "Operating income = gross profit − operating expenses, so it can't exceed gross profit. Costco: gross 12.8%, operating 3.8%.",
              "source": {
                "ticker": "COST",
                "fy": 2025,
                "metrics": [
                  "gross_margin",
                  "operating_margin"
                ],
                "formula": "operating_income / revenue"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "q-u1l2-4",
              "type": "compare",
              "prompt": "Which chipmaker had the higher net margin in its latest year?",
              "choices": [
                "NVDA",
